[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known as one bug. Read by tenant and by what the reports say, it holds three problems.
Each now has its own ticket. The counts below are computed from the export on every build.

<SplitTable ticket={4471} tickets={{ parser: `${repo}/1`, hint: `${repo}/2`, 'one-day': `${repo}/3` }} />

## The three problems

**`parser` — the shared parser reads every date month first.** Day-first tenants get day and month
swapped: "7 April" goes out as "4 July". This is what #4471's title describes, and its queued fix
covers only this.

**`hint` — booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** At day-first tenants on
booking-v3, people type what the hint says, month first, and the form reads it day first. It
looks like the parser bug in the report, but the parser fix will not touch it: the form's hint and
its reading must agree.

**`one-day` — the date moves by one day, not a month flip.** Tuesday shows as Monday, an invite
arrives before the booking, two clients in different time zones get different days for the same
meeting. That is a time-zone or day-boundary bug. The desk noted these reports
(`desk-notes.json`) but [the #4471 table](/kb/incidents/4471) counts them under `parser`.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not count by intake tag. Intake guesses the cause from the reporter's browser; many reports
come from browsers set to <code>en-US</code> at day-first tenants. The cause follows the tenant's
locale, its booking form and the channel (<code>causes.ts</code>), and the "intake tag differs"
column shows how often the guess is wrong.
</Callout>

## How this was counted

1. Drop repeated rows: the export pages overlap, so one id counts once (`uniqueById`).
2. Take the desk's one-day list first; those reports are `one-day`.
3. Place every other report with `causeOf`: day-first tenant, `form` channel, booking-v3 → `hint`; any
   other day-first report → `parser`.

## What to change on the desk

- Split by cause, not subject. Same subject, different cause: keep apart. The
  [dedupe explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) already shows the difference.
- When a big ticket is marked known, check that its fix covers every report in it.

